Package: quant2qual
Title: The Automated Behavioral Narrator: Turn Behavioral Metrics into
    Qualitative Case-Study Prose
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bernard Isekah", "Osangir", , "b.osangir@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Neudata Consulting Ltd", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: Bridges quantitative behavioral data and qualitative case-study
    reporting. Numeric distributions of time, activity and friction (for
    example clickstreams, app metrics, learning-platform logs or survey
    paradata) are standardised against their own cohort, banded with
    user-defined or distribution-based thresholds, and mapped onto a
    configurable matrix of behavioral archetypes with rule-based or fuzzy
    membership and an explicit classification confidence. A rule-based,
    fully local narrative engine then translates each profile into
    clinical, user-experience or brief analytical prose that cites its own
    evidence (percentiles, cohort ratios, outliers) and states its own
    uncertainty. Cohort narratives and complete case-study reports can be
    written as Markdown, R Markdown or Quarto sources, or rendered to HTML
    and to PDF in the Neudata house style. No external API is required.
